  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the LOT-133 tests, I want a captured `rss.php` answer that holds an item raised in forum 25 (the Apple category), so that the category-25 rule (Q-7) is tested on a real answer instead of a captured item whose `cat` was changed.\n\n### Scope\n\n- LOT-133 ([#223](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/223), PR #1001) hides items whose link has `cat=25` for the logged-out viewer and the review account. `T01` (run 10, [#133](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/133)) has 23 links with a `cat`, none is 25, so the tests derive one (`QualityAlertsTestSupport.inForum25`) and say so.\n- Capture `rss.php` (no cookie, no account) at a moment its 25 items include one with `cat=25`; store it as the next `T` number of the corpus with its meta, anonymized per `docs/FIXTURES.md`. If the live feed never holds one, say so on this issue and close it: the derived value stays.\n- Same capture if possible: an item whose reporter comment holds an HTML entity (already pending in [#438](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/438); do not duplicate, answer there).\n- Not to capture: anything that writes to AQ.\n\n### Wants this capture\n\n- LOT-133 (#223)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A capture with its meta, anonymized, that `AQFeedParser` reads, with a `cat=25` link.\n- [ ] `QualityAlertsVisibilityTests` reads it instead of the derived item (follow-up PR, not this issue).",
